{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1575","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L. Longest Array Deconstruction"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Mr. Chanek gives you a sequence $$$a$$$ indexed from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$. Define $$$f(a)$$$ as the number of indices where $$$a_i = i$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can pick an element from the current sequence and remove it, then concatenate the remaining elements together. For example, if you remove the $$$3$$$-rd element from the sequence $$$[4, 2, 3, 1]$$$, the resulting sequence will be $$$[4, 2, 1]$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You want to remove some elements from $$$a$$$ in order to maximize $$$f(a)$$$, using zero or more operations. Find the largest possible $$$f(a)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains one integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the initial length of the sequence."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\leq a_i \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the initial sequence $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output an integer denoting the largest $$$f(a)$$$ that can be obtained by doing zero or more operations."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7\n2 1 4 2 5 3 7\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n4 2 3 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, $$$f(A) = 3$$$ by doing the following operations."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$[2,1,\\textbf{4},2,5,3,7] \\rightarrow [\\textbf{2},1,2,5,3,7] \\rightarrow [1,2,5,3,\\textbf{7}] \\rightarrow [1,2,\\textbf{5},3] \\rightarrow [1,2,3]$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, $$$f(A) = 2$$$ and no additional operation is needed."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"L","problemCode":"1575L","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1575/problem/L"}